    "document_summary": "AIA Hospital Income is a hospital cash plan intended to pay a daily cash allowance during hospitalisation and recovery to cover “unexpected extras” that may not be fully covered by your existing hospitalisation plan. It pays different cash benefits based on where/when the insured event occurs: a Daily Hospital Income Benefit of S$100/day (Plan 1), S$200/day (Plan 2), or S$300/day (Plan 3) up to 500 days; an Intensive Care Unit Income Benefit (on top of Daily Hospital Income) of S$300/day (Plan 1), S$450/day (Plan 2), or S$750/day (Plan 3) up to 30 days; and additional recovery supports such as Get Well Benefit, Post-hospitalisation Home Rest (up to 5 days), and Day Surgery Income Benefit. Premiums vary by entry age and plan, and the brochure states premium rates are not guaranteed.",
